.TH WIFI-DIAG 1 "October 26, 2026" "homebrew-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wifi-diag \- one\-screen network diagnostics for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wifi-diag
[\fB\-j\fR] [\fB\-i\fR \fIIF\fR] [\fB\-t\fR \fIHOST\fR] [\fB\-d\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-network\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wifi-diag
summarises the active network connection using only commands that ship
with macOS:
.BR route (8),
.BR ipconfig (8),
.BR networksetup (8),
.BR scutil (8),
.BR dscacheutil (1),
.BR ping (8)
and
.BR curl (1).
It never needs sudo and never changes the configuration.
.PP
It reports the default\-route interface and its hardware port, the Wi\-Fi
network name, the IPv4 address, the gateway and the DNS servers of the
primary resolver, then runs five checks: default route, gateway latency,
internet latency, name resolution and captive portal.
.PP
Recent macOS versions hide the Wi\-Fi network name from processes without
Location Services. wifi\-diag then reports it as hidden instead of failing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the report as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fIIF\fR
Inspect \fIIF\fR instead of the default\-route interface.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " " \fIHOST\fR
Host for the internet latency probe. Default 1.1.1.1.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dns\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name to resolve for the DNS check. Default apple.com.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
Pings per probe. Default 3.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-network
Skip the active probes (ping, DNS lookup, captive portal request).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every check passed.
.TP
.B 1
At least one check is degraded: gateway above 30 ms, internet above 150 ms,
packet loss, or a captive portal.
.TP
.B 2
No connectivity: no default route, or a probe got no answer.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error.
.TP
.B 69
Not macOS, or a required system command is missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wifi\-diag
wifi\-diag \-\-json | jq '.checks[] | select(.status != "ok")'
wifi\-diag \-\-no\-network \-\-interface en1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR networksetup (8),
.BR scutil (8),
.BR ping (8)
